      "textEn": "231.\nBrahma-bhutah - attained the state of Brahma, the form-siddha, by remaining silent; Tushnim - by remaining silent; Shibikam - palanquin; Purva-vat - as before;\nUvah - taken away. King Rahugana said to Jad Bharat: My brother, this is so painful! You are definitely very\ntired, because you have been carrying a palanquin alone for a long time and from a long distance without anyone's help.\nYou are bringing the palanquin alone. Besides, you're troubled at heart by your old self. Hey,\nFriend, I can see that you are neither fat nor skinny. Are the Kahar with you\nNot cooperating with you? In this way, the king taunted Jad Bharat, but even so, Jad Bharat was not aware of his body.\nHe was not conscious. He knew that he was not the body, because he had become one with the form. He was neither\nSo fat, nor thin, nor did he have any connection with this gross matter of five gross elements and three subtle elements.\nHe had nothing to do with it. He had no concern with the physical body and its two hands and two feet.\nIn other words, if one wants to say, one can say that he had attained 'Aham Brahmasmi', that is, the form of Brahma. Therefore, the king's satirical criticism had no effect on him. He, without\nsaying anything, continued to lift the palanquin as before. Meaning: Jad Bharat was completely free. Even when the dacoits wanted to sacrifice their bodies,\nthey did not care, because they knew that they are not bodies. Even if their body is destroyed,\nthey do not care, because they had complete faith in this saying of the Bhagavad Gita—Na hanyate\nHanyamane Shareere—that it is not destroyed. They knew that even if the body is killed, they cannot be killed.\nCannot be killed. Although he did not object, the perfect Supreme Lord, towards his devotee,\ncould not bear this injustice of the robbers, therefore the robbers were killed, and by the grace of Shri Krishna, they\nescaped. Even while carrying the palanquin, they knew that they were not bodies.\nHis body was fully capable of carrying the palanquin,\nbecause he was healthy, strong, and well-built. Due to being free from the sense of the body,\nKing's satire, a special type of words, had no effect on him. The origin of the body\nis according to karma, and nature gathers all the materials for the development of a particular type of body.\nIt gathers. The soul within the body is separate from the body's structure. Therefore, anything done towards the body"
