      "textEn": "241\n\nThe king was also equal to the sages in the lineage of the Guru. In ancient times, the Rajarshi understood the philosophy of life and\nknew how to educate the citizens to rise to that level. That is, they knew how to free citizens from the bondage of birth\nand death. When Maharaj Dashrath was ruling in Ayodhya,\nOnce Maharishi Vishwamitra came to ask for Ramchandra and Lakshman to be taken to the forest for the killing of the demons.\nFor that purpose. When Vishwamitra Muni Maharaj came to Dasharatha's court, to welcome him,\nhe asked him—Aihishtam yat tat punarjanmajayaya—That is, to win over the cycle of birth and death,\nare his efforts going well? The entire process of Vedic civilization is based on this fact. We\nshould know how to win over the cycle of birth and death. Even Maharaj Rahugan\nknew the goal of life, therefore when the inert Bharat presented the philosophy of life before him, then he\nimmediately praised it. It is the foundation of Vedic society.\nScholars, Brahmins, saints, and sages\nwere familiar with Vedic purposes, therefore they used to preach to kings for the welfare of the common people. In this way, the community benefited from their cooperation. Therefore, success was achieved in every object. Maharaj Rahugan was fully aware of the importance of human life, therefore he was sorry for the harsh words spoken by him to Jad.\nBharat. He immediately got down from the palanquin and fell at the feet of Jad Bharat,\nasked for forgiveness, and prayed to know more about the importance of life, which is called Brahma Jigyasa. The high officials of this time are completely unaware of the life values, therefore when\nsaints want to spread Vedic knowledge, they do not even greet them and\ncreate obstacles in the propagation of spiritual knowledge. Thus, it can be said that ancient\npolitical rule was like heaven, and the current rule is like hell. Who are you, mysterious and inaccessible, O Brahmin?\nWho is the one who wields 